<!--Post: 170--><!--Time: 1086298367-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST170"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, June 03, 2004 - 2:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think the unidentified baby picture looks very much like Shirley Vian or someone related? Compare the pictures, especially their noses.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 170-->
<!--Post: 189--><!--Time: 1086360307-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST189"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Warren_b<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Warren_b<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 04, 2004 - 7:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yea &#39;Book!  You&#39;re back!  It seems to be the consensus at Kansas.com and the C&amp;J Board that the baby picture is Shirley Vian.  Behind that, one of the Oteros.  What I&#39;m curious about is why he would send a picture of one of his known victims &#40;they did not know BTK was the killer  when he sent the Wegerle pictures&#41;. The party line is that the only thing he sent was the baby picture itself.  We are left to speculate if he sent a message, and/or whether that message was in the corner of the photograph that was cut off. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 189-->
<!--Post: 191--><!--Time: 1086365269-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST191"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Muskogee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Muskogee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 04, 2004 - 9:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe the picture &#40;if truly sent by BTK&#41; IS of an unknown victim...Perhaps BTK is sending it both as proof that he was in the house of this person at some point, and for victim identification purposes.  <BR> <BR>Perhaps this was sent in after a request from the WPD for more &#34;evidence&#34; of who he was.  Hmmmm...anyone in Witchita see any strange personal ads lately?  <BR> <BR>And I still like Doug&#39;s theory that the baby looks like she could be Hispanic/Native American.  This causes me to speculate that it could have been taken from the Otero house.  However, I wouldn&#39;t rule anything out...I think it could be Shirly Vian, as well.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 191-->
<!--Post: 195--><!--Time: 1086382139-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST195"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Laoise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Laoise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 04, 2004 - 1:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://genforum.genealogy.com/vian/messages/107.html" target=_top>http://genforum.genealogy.com/vian/messages/107.ht ml</a> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 195-->
<!--Post: 196--><!--Time: 1086382329-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST196"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 04, 2004 - 1:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here&#39;s the text version of the above link in case it gets deleted. It was posted by a David Bell: <BR> <BR><i>Friends, <BR>KSNW - TV in Wichita, KS recently recieved an unidentified baby photo. That photo may be of a woman named Shirley Vian. Ms. Vian lived in Wichita and was murdered in 1977 by the serial killer known as BTK. <BR> <BR>So far we have been unable to find any relatives of Ms. Vian in the Wichita area. In fact, police used a non-relative to identify Shirley&#39;s body when it was found. <BR> <BR>If you knew Shirley Vian of Wichita, Kansas and can identify her baby picture please contact me at <a href="mailto:dbell@ksn.com">dbell@ksn.com</a> <BR> <BR>Thank you.</i> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 196-->
<!--Post: 197--><!--Time: 1086390831-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST197"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Debbie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Debbie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 04, 2004 - 4:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Shirley is buried in Oklahoma under the name of Relford &#40;all her kids had that name, I believe&#41; <BR><a href="http://www.rootsweb.com/~okleflor/cemetery/muse.htm" target=_top>http://www.rootsweb.com/~okleflor/cemetery/muse.ht m</a> <BR>Relford Shirley 22 Nov 1951 17 Mar 1977 39AA  <BR> <BR>Her maiden name was Lawson. Maybe the picture would be better off on genealogy website with one of those names.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 197-->
<!--Post: 198--><!--Time: 1086392093-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST198"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 04, 2004 - 4:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The outfit the baby has on looks more like a boys knit set with a doggy picture on it. At first I was thought the baby was a boy. <BR> <BR>This was on the crime library site. Maybe the picture is the one of the pictures mentioned here: <BR> <BR>&#34;The killer had stopped one of the victim&#39;s &#40;Shirley&#41; sons on the street that morning, and showed him photographs of a woman and child, purportedly seeking directions to their home.&#34; <BR><a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolved/btk/them_3.html?sect=4" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolve d/btk/them_3.html?sect=4</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 198-->
<!--Post: 199--><!--Time: 1086393452-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST199"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 04, 2004 - 4:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very good theory, Bookworm. I hadn&#39;t considered that angle.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 199-->
<!--Post: 201--><!--Time: 1086397163-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST201"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 04, 2004 - 5:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If it is a boy, then maybe the pic is of BTK himself.  If so, that might suggest that he has no close living relatives who might easily identify him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 201-->
<!--Post: 211--><!--Time: 1086493494-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST211"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, June 05, 2004 - 8:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I can&#39;t believe my eyes ! You two have to be pulling bookworms leg or something,we had this very discussion a few weeks ago,even the fact that he has no living relatives,so he could put his baby picture out there.But then you both had a few beers,and I didn&#39;t. It has to be the btk,what fun would it be other wise ? Bookworm, I am the person on the other site who said I thought it was a boys outfit, with a puppy dog on it and its tongue hanging out.The curl on his head was something that we mothers did, because we thought it was so cute. We did the same for the girls but they had to have bow&#39;s,and fancy dress&#39;s.At first I felt he was older than 6mos.But now I think 6mos.is about right for a picture of a baby,next would be one yr.old. picture. Well I am glad we have that one solved !<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 211-->
<!--Post: 213--><!--Time: 1086500886-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST213"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Unsub<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Unsub<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, June 05, 2004 - 10:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The domain for the person who posted the photo is for KSN which appears to be the local NBC affliate. I think they are the station that received the photo. It was on thier site for a while asking for any information, then was taken off with no information given as to why. <BR> <BR>However I did have a new thought reading this. I always figured the corner piece that was missing had some sort of info on it that the sender didnt want seen so they cropped it. <BR> <BR>What if instead the corner had the BTK signature, rumored to be on all his letters and was removed by the station/polce before put on the stations website ? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 213-->
<!--Post: 225--><!--Time: 1086700142-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST225"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 08, 2004 - 6:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sandy, <BR>I agree on the age of 6 mo. The sweater outfit probably meant that the picture was taken at a cool time of the year starting September to about April when they start wearing Spring clothes. The baby could have been born from March through September or October? <BR> <BR>They didn&#39;t say if one the pictures the children were shown was of Shirley or if the picture was a baby. Maybe BTK was adopted.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 225-->
<!--Post: 226--><!--Time: 1086706339-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST226"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Warren_b<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Warren_b<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 08, 2004 - 7:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My recollection on the discussions at C&amp;J is that the photo was mailed to the station, and at first, they thought it was from someone who sent it in to honor a birthday, which the TV station does.  Yet they put no note, nor was there a return address.  The best theory is that it is Shirley Vian, and she has very few relatives, if any.  No one that we know of has come forward to ID the photo.   I doubt the station or police cut the corner off &#40;and it appears it was cut, and not overlaid&#41; as that would be tampering with evidence somewhat.  And cut corners apparently were a signature in BTK communications.  I&#39;m sure this is redundant, and I&#39;m just encapsulating it in my mind; have to defer to our fair women, such as Sandy and Musk&#39; as to sex and age &#40;and especially if they&#39;d like some sex with the aged - sorry&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 226-->
<!--Post: 230--><!--Time: 1086807799-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST230"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, June 09, 2004 - 12:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If the TV station learned it was a hoax, it&#39;s doubtful they would announce they had been duped, especially after giving the story so much attention. Most likely they would do exactly as they did; simply remove the picture quietly from their website. <BR> <BR>BTK put a secret mark on all of his letters, so if this one didn&#39;t have it... <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t have any insider info, just speculating.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 230-->
<!--Post: 235--><!--Time: 1086830222-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST235"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Doone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Doone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, June 09, 2004 - 6:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why would BTK send in a handwritten envelope with an enclosed unidentified baby photo?  Yes, it seems he loves delivering the bad news, so what would this photo mean?  I feel he has too much ego to be that vague.  A baby pic is too flat for his tastes.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 235-->
<!--Post: 236--><!--Time: 1086831594-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST236"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, June 09, 2004 - 6:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Unless you are a nut case like the btk,how could you understand anything he does ? If that picture is him, then it is like in your face---Here I am, bet you still can&#39;t find me !<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 236-->
<!--Post: 275--><!--Time: 1087144931-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST275"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, June 13, 2004 - 9:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Looking at the hands of the child in the baby picture, I was wondering how a baby could hold a hand pose like that.  Unless the baby&#39;s hands are tied with a knit-like tie, which is a different color from the sweater sleeves. Notice how the thumbs are crossed. <BR> <BR>BTK bound his first victims, so its not like he saw this picture and decided to bind his victims. Unless he had the picture before he began his killings. That&#39;s if the baby&#39;s hands are bound for the pose.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 275-->
<!--Post: 276--><!--Time: 1087150116-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST276"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ryan_olesin<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ryan_olesin<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, June 13, 2004 - 11:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does anyone know what that logo is on the baby&#39;s outfit?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 276-->
<!--Post: 277--><!--Time: 1087156240-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST277"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, June 13, 2004 - 12:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->We have discussed that a few times over at Zodiackiller.com. Everybody is seeing different things, although most agree the last three letters appear to be &#34;OUL&#34;.Was able to enlarge it a bit, but still nothing definite. Looks like DOZ_OUL. I think the large letter is an &#34;S&#34;. <BR> Can you do anything with it, that&#39;s your territory? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 277-->
<!--Post: 279--><!--Time: 1087158672-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST279"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Muskogee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Muskogee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, June 13, 2004 - 1:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Doug and Sean did a fantastic job trying to identify what it is/what it says.  Sandy suggested a dog face, which I can see, except I don&#39;t see the ears.  I originally suggested &#34;Wise as an owl,&#34; or &#34;Quiet as an owl,&#34; &#40;only being able to read part of the saying&#41; and an &#34;owl face.&#34;  There also appear to be little crescent moons on the outfit.  Since then, the enhancements/enlargements Sean and Doug have done make me feel relatively certain the next-to-last letter is a &#34;u&#34; rather than a &#34;w,&#34; so that would blow that theory away. Still, I&#39;d be interested to hear others&#39; takes on the idea. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 279-->
<!--Post: 281--><!--Time: 1087159895-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST281"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ryan_olesin<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ryan_olesin<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, June 13, 2004 - 1:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It looks like &#39;iRac_h&#39; <BR>Whatever the hell that is.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 281-->
<!--Post: 284--><!--Time: 1087185116-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST284"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitaboy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitaboy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, June 13, 2004 - 8:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It is a caricature of a beaver.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 284-->
<!--Post: 286--><!--Time: 1087227904-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST286"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Swa<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Swa<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, June 14, 2004 - 8:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Where can we view this photo? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 286-->
<!--Post: 287--><!--Time: 1087231332-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST287"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, June 14, 2004 - 9:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s one of the last entries on the &#34;History&#34; page of this site.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 287-->
<!--Post: 486--><!--Time: 1089864529-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST486"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, July 14, 2004 - 9:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My guess is that it is a bunny rabbit. Look at the bottom of the mouth and you will see what looks like buggs bunny type buck teeth. Only one ear is showing because the other ear is covered by the baby&#39;s sweater being bunched up.   <BR>-Deb<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 486-->
<!--Post: 619--><!--Time: 1090955213-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST619"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Clarice<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Clarice<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 27, 2004 - 12:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sean, I miss that zodiak.com site for BTK. I remember the discussion well<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 619-->
<!--Post: 649--><!--Time: 1091142553-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST649"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, July 29, 2004 - 4:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bookworm, Children at that age are just learning to put their hands together.  It is fun for them to interlock their fingers, once they know that they can do it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 649-->
<!--Post: 685--><!--Time: 1091495071-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST685"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, August 02, 2004 - 6:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Sandy, <BR>Well maybe, but I still think it looks posed.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 685-->
<!--Post: 917--><!--Time: 1093574853-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST917"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Laoise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Laoise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 26, 2004 - 7:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just to add my 2 cents here: I personally think that pic looks like a stork baby carrying cloth thing.... did that make sense?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 917-->
<!--Post: 998--><!--Time: 1094444553-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST998"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Slatz<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Slatz<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, September 05, 2004 - 9:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think the baby is posed to look like he/she is praying. What do you guys think?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 998-->
<!--Post: 1001--><!--Time: 1094528131-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1001"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, September 06, 2004 - 8:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Slatz, I don&#39;t think you can get a baby at that age to pose.I would think that the photographer took more than one picture of the baby,this just happens to be the one that was sent. Could be the mother liked this one because it did looked like the baby was praying. They could be catholic,it was once believed that the Z was catholic because of his need to confess. I have seen a Z like logo used in the catholic church worn by the priest.It can also be seen in the  &#34;Exorist the Begining&#34; film on the scarf worn by the priest in the movie.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1001-->
<!--Post: 1677--><!--Time: 1102583323-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1677"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 09, 2004 - 1:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The photo of the baby with the beaver/boxing gloves &#40;speculated&#41; on it&#39;s sweater looks like Shirley Vian.  <BR> <BR>A lot!  <BR> <BR>If you super-impose the two photos over each other they match up.  <BR> <BR>Look at their noses.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1677-->
